{"content":[{"c":["DROPSY*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Old medical term for excessive accumulation of watery fluid in any tissue or space of the body. Dropsy, mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.14.2","r":"Luke.14.2","rawR":"Luke.14.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.14.2","value":"Luke.14.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 14:2"},", is a symptom of several serious disorders such as heart, kidney, or liver disease; Jesus healed a man “who had dropsy” but whose underlying illness is not described. The word “dropsy” has generally been replaced with more specific medical terms: excessive abdominal fluid is now referred to as ascites, cutaneous or subcutaneous dropsy as edema, and pleural dropsy as hydrothorax. Dropsy is not mentioned directly in the OT. A reference to swollen feet (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.8.4","r":"Deut.8.4","rawR":"Deut.8.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.8.4","value":"Deut.8.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 8:4"},") could refer to pedal edema or simply to the formation of blisters."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Medicine and Medical Practice"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Dropsy","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Luke 14:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.14.2","rawQueryValue":"Luke.14.2","sourceRefExact":"Luke.14.2"},{"anchorText":"Dt 8:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.8.4","rawQueryValue":"Deut.8.4","sourceRefExact":"Deut.8.4"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5d9bb444d22259369e7f791e0c85d6cd4a692ce001882e2d908baa3d03f3c2ba","sourceItemName":"Dropsy","sourceItemOrder":169,"sourceMember":"Articles/D.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Dropsy","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Dropsy*","title":"Dropsy*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}